Rule 1 (both inputs must be valid torch dtype codes [0..10])
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= (v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10) ∧ (v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 2 (neither input may be a string or numpy dtype sentinel code [11, 12])
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [11, 12] : (v_1 ≠ i ∧ v_2 ≠ i)
>>
Rule 3 (dtype codes are integral values)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= (v_1 % 1 = 0) ∧ (v_2 % 1 = 0)
>>
Rule 4 (if any input is complex-coded [9..10], both must still be valid dtype codes)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= if ((v_1 ≥ 9 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10) ∨ (v_2 ≥ 9 ∧ v_2 ≤ 10)) then ((v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 10) ∧ (v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ 10))
>>
Rule 5 (each input must exist within the allowed dtype index domain)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : dtype} |= ∃i ∈ [0, 10] : (v_1 = i) ∧ ∃j ∈ [0, 10] : (v_2 = j)
